abstract: "A bounded Rust experiment combining extracted PD, ERA/KiE scientific computation and a source-derived one-use FFI gate with new scoped memory and storage adapters. Five fresh-process cycles preserve complete operation records, reconstructed memory and exact PD checkpoint bytes against controls. One supported proposition and one countered proposition coexist, each with two occurrence references. Local validation comprises 50 root tests and 19 separately executed science tests, with zero failures or ignored tests, plus a passing locked offline release build. The numerical example is a SOFA/sofars conformance-model comparison, not independent physical observation. Full native knowledge_verdict remains null; valid older history is accepted, finite bounds and source-version dependence remain explicit. The legacy FFI write surface remains no-write CompatibilityHold; a new borrowed callback delegates recomputation and storage to its owner. Apache-2.0 applies to the capsule with retained third-party MIT/SOFA obligations. Human architectural direction and AI-assisted engineering are disclosed."
